Every tool declares a JSON Schema that is handed verbatim to the providers, so the schema the model was given is also the contract its call must meet. `ToolRegistry.execute` is the one place that can hold the model to it: validation happens there, before the executor runs, and a rejected call comes back to the model as a tool result it can read and correct — not as a thrown error that ends the conversation.

